{"type":"text","timestamp":1788383771197,"sessionID":"ses_f9c0a861affeswRxO5BoLkpFPB","part":{"id":"prt_063faac31001K06Tg41bnuw8hr","messageID":"msg_063faa9d2001veaCNYXOqh6R9T","sessionID":"ses_f9c0a861affeswRxO5BoLkpFPB","type":"text","text":"Done. The book collection REST API is implemented in TypeScript + Express + SQLite (`better-sqlite3`), builds cleanly (`tsc --noEmit` passes), and all 12 tests pass.\n\n**Files created:**\n- `package.json` / `tsconfig.json` — project + strict TS config\n- `src/types.ts` — `Book`/`BookInput` interfaces\n- `src/db.ts` — SQLite data layer (prepared statements, `:memory:` or file)\n- `src/app.ts` — `createApp()` Express factory with all routes + validation + JSON error handling\n- `src/server.ts` — entry point (`PORT`, `DB_PATH` env vars, graceful shutdown)\n- `tests/books.test.ts` — 12 integration tests via `node:test` + `supertest` against in-memory SQLite\n- `README.md` / `.gitignore`\n\n**Endpoints:** `GET /health`, `POST /books`, `GET /books` (with `?author=` filter), `GET /books/:id`, `PUT /books/:id`, `DELETE /books/:id` — returning JSON with `200/201/204/400/404` status codes; title & author are required/validated.\n\nVerified end-to-end: `npm run build` → exit 0, `npm test` → 12/12 pass, and a live `node dist/src/server.js` smoke run returned correct status codes for every endpoint. Run with `npm install && npm start` (see README for usage).","time":{"start":1788383767601,"end":1788383771191}}}
